Manual review corrections (first review pass), none upstream-source-specific --
these are typographic/LaTeX-quality fixes to the converter's otherwise
faithful transcription:

- Exercise 15's "$a\,\text{and}\,b$" (parallelogram sides) and its (a)/(b)/(c)
  sub-list ("Side a" / "Side b" / "$\text{Angle}\,\theta$") mixed bare prose
  variables with an ad-hoc `\text{and}` join; unwrapped to plain prose with
  the variables in math mode: "$a$ and $b$", "Side $a$", "Side $b$",
  "Angle $\theta$" -- consistent with this repo's convention of keeping
  English outside math mode.
- Two further instances of the same "$n\,\text{and}\,R$" / "$x\,\text{and}\,y$"
  pattern (the pressure-function exercise and the Cobb-Douglas exercise)
  fixed the same way, to "$n$ and $R$" / "$x$ and $y$".
- The heat-flow exercise's "$xy\text{-plane}$" glued the variable pair and
  the word "-plane" into one math span; unwrapped to "$xy$-plane".
- The heat-equation exercise ("Show that $z=e^{-t}\cos(\frac{x}{c})$
  satisfies the heat equation ...") was missing its terminal sentence
  period after the closing display; added.
